      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2024-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Factoring, \\(2024=2^3\\cdot11\\cdot23.\\) The factorial \\(n!\\) contains the prime \\(23\\) only when \\(n\\ge23.\\) At \\(n=23,\\) the product \\(23!\\) already includes \\(23,\\ 11,\\) and plenty of factors of \\(2,\\) so \\(23!\\) is a multiple of \\(2024.\\) Thus, the correct answer is D.",
